---
/**
 * Privacy Policy — a notice describing this site's actual data practices,
 * not legal advice given to the visitor. Internal notes on legal review,
 * governing-law language, and entity status live in
 * docs/content-rights-checklist.md, not on this public page.
 *
 * Identifies the operator as "The Electric Lavender Train" only — no LLC,
 * corporate, or registered-entity status is claimed anywhere on this page,
 * because nothing in this repository verifies one.
 */

import LegalPage from "../layouts/LegalPage.astro";
import siteConfig, { formatPageTitle } from "../data/siteConfig";

const title = formatPageTitle("Privacy Policy");
const description = `How ${siteConfig.bandNameFormal} collects, uses, and protects information submitted through this website.`;
const email = siteConfig.contact.email;
---

<LegalPage
  title={title}
  description={description}
  kicker="Legal"
  heading="Privacy Policy"
  effectiveDate="August 15, 2026"
>
  <p>
    This website is operated by The Electric Lavender Train (“we,” “us,” or “our”). This Privacy
    Policy explains what information we collect through this website, why we collect it, who we
    share it with, and the choices you have.
  </p>

  <h2>Information you provide to us</h2>
  <p>
    This site has three inquiry forms on the <a href={siteConfig.routes.contactBooking}>Contact
    & Booking</a> page: <strong>Booking Inquiry</strong>, <strong>Merch Inquiry</strong>, and 
    <strong> Other</strong>. What you submit depends on which form you use:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>Booking Inquiry:</strong> name and email (required); phone, organization or venue,
      preferred date, and estimated audience size (optional); event type and event location
      (required — location asks only for “city and venue, if known,” not a street address); event
      details (required).
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Merch Inquiry:</strong> name, email, and the merchandise item you're asking about
      (required); quantity/size/other details (optional); your message (required).
    </li>
    <li><strong>Other:</strong> name, email, and subject (required); your message (required).</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    Every field on these forms is plain text. There are no file uploads anywhere on this site, and
    we ask that you not include payment card numbers, government identification numbers, or
    medical information in any of these forms — a reminder to that effect appears directly above
    the forms themselves.
  </p>
  <p>
    If you email us directly at <a href={`mailto:${email}`}>{email}</a> instead of using a form,
    that message and whatever you choose to include in it is handled the same way any email is
    handled by Gmail/Google, described further below.
  </p>

  <h2>Information collected automatically</h2>
  <p>
    When you submit one of the forms above, our form-delivery provider, <strong>Formspree</strong>,
    may automatically receive standard technical information along with your submission — such as
    your IP address, browser and device information, the time of submission, and the page that
    referred you to the form. This is typical of how web forms function and is not something we
    configure separately; it comes from Formspree's own processing of the request. We do not use
    this technical information to build an advertising profile of you.
  </p>
  <p>
    This website's hosting provider (expected to be Netlify, though the final choice of host may
    change before launch) may also log standard web-server access information — such as IP
    address, requested pages, and timestamps — as part of ordinary hosting operations, independent
    of anything you submit through a form.
  </p>

  <h2>How we use your information</h2>
  <p>We use the information you submit to:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>Respond to booking, merchandise, and general inquiries;</li>
    <li>Communicate with you about an inquiry or, where applicable, a confirmed booking;</li>
    <li>Identify and prevent spam and abusive submissions; and</li>
    <li>Maintain records reasonably necessary for our business, accounting, or legal purposes.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    We do <strong>not</strong> sell your information, and we do not use inquiry information for
    behavioral advertising.
  </p>

  <h2>Service providers we use</h2>
  <p>The following third-party services are involved in operating this website and handling inquiries:</p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Formspree</strong> — receives, processes, and may store the contents of form submissions, and delivers them to us by email. Formspree has its own privacy practices, which you can review at their website.</li>
    <li><strong>Gmail / Google</strong> — the email service where inquiry notifications and any direct emails to <a href={`mailto:${email}`}>{email}</a> are received and stored.</li>
    <li><strong>Our website host</strong> — serves the website itself and may log standard access information as described above.</li>
    <li><strong>Sanity</strong> — the content platform used to manage and publish this website's public editorial content (such as band photos, event listings, and merchandise descriptions). Sanity does not receive or store anything you submit through the contact forms.</li>
    <li><strong>YouTube</strong> — used to embed video content on this site, including the featured video and the Media &amp; Merch gallery videos. See “Embedded YouTube videos” below.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Marketing communications</h2>
  <p>
    We do not automatically add anyone who submits an inquiry to a marketing or newsletter list. If
    we ever introduce email marketing in the future, we will only send it to people who have given a
    separate, explicit, unchecked opt-in specifically for that purpose — never simply because they
    once submitted a booking, merchandise, or general inquiry.
  </p>

  <h2>Analytics and advertising</h2>
  <p>
    At launch, this website does not use Google Analytics, Meta Pixel, or any other analytics,
    advertising, or remarketing tracking technology. If that changes in the future, this Privacy
    Policy — and, where required, our approach to cookie consent — will be updated first.
  </p>

  <h2>Cookies and similar technologies</h2>
  <p>
    We do not configure analytics cookies, behavioral-advertising cookies, or remarketing trackers of
    any kind on this website. We are not able to promise that no cookie or similar local storage will
    ever be set by any part of this site or the third-party services it embeds — for example, YouTube
    may set its own cookies once you choose to activate an embedded video, as part of its own normal
    operation (see below) — but nothing along those lines is configured by us, and we do not use
    cookies to build an advertising profile of visitors.
  </p>

  <h2>Embedded YouTube videos</h2>
  <p>
    YouTube videos on this site — including the featured video and the videos in the Media &amp;
    Merch photo/video gallery — are embedded using YouTube's privacy-enhanced mode
    (<code>youtube-nocookie.com</code>), and the video player itself is never loaded until you
    actively click to play it — simply visiting a page with an embedded video does not load anything
    from YouTube. Once you choose to play a video, you're interacting directly with YouTube's own
    player, which YouTube (owned by Google) operates according to its own privacy policy and terms.
    YouTube may show advertising within the embedded player. YouTube states that advertising shown
    through privacy-enhanced mode is non-personalized — we report that as YouTube's own stated
    behavior, not as our own guarantee of how Google's systems actually operate. YouTube still
    processes information about your interaction with the activated player according to its own
    practices, which we do not control or fully disclose. To be clear, this is entirely separate
    from the "no analytics, behavioral advertising, or remarketing trackers" statement above, which
    describes what <em>we</em> configure on this website — it does not, and could not, override how
    YouTube's own embedded product behaves once activated.
  </p>

  <h2>Data retention</h2>
  <p>
    We generally retain inquiry information for up to 12 months after our last interaction with
    you. We may retain certain information longer when reasonably necessary to complete a booking,
    maintain business or financial records, resolve a dispute, enforce an agreement, or comply with
    legal obligations. Spam and unnecessary information may be deleted sooner. Deletion under this
    policy is a manual review-and-remove process, not an automated one.
  </p>

  <h2>Your rights and choices</h2>
  <p>
    You may request access to, correction of, or deletion of information you've submitted to us by
    emailing <a href={`mailto:${email}`}>{email}</a>. What we can do depends on where the information
    lives:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>Submissions stored in our Formspree account</strong> and <strong>notifications and
      conversations in our Gmail account</strong> are ours to locate and delete, and we will do so
      for a valid request (subject to the retention exceptions above — e.g. records tied to a
      confirmed booking).
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Any spreadsheet or other export</strong> we've made from the above is likewise ours to
      delete, and is held to the same retention rules as the original.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Provider-controlled security logs, records we're legally required to keep, and
      backups</strong> our providers retain as part of their own disaster-recovery practices are
      outside our direct control — we can ask our providers to remove them, but cannot guarantee
      the exact timing of that deletion.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Security</h2>
  <p>
    We take reasonable steps to protect information submitted through this website, including
    relying on our providers' own security practices (such as Formspree's and Google's). No method
    of transmission or storage over the internet is completely secure, and we cannot guarantee
    absolute security.
  </p>

  <h2>Children's privacy</h2>
  <p>
    This website and its forms are not directed to children under 13, and we do not knowingly
    collect personal information from children under 13. If you believe a child has submitted
    information to us, please contact us at <a href={`mailto:${email}`}>{email}</a> so we can
    address it.
  </p>

  <h2>California privacy disclosures</h2>
  <p>
    For California residents: the categories of personal information we collect are limited to
    what's described above — identifiers (name, email, phone if provided) and the content of your
    inquiry. We do not sell this information, and we share it only with the service providers
    listed above, for the purposes described above — not for cross-context behavioral advertising.
    This website does not currently respond differently to browser "Do Not Track" signals or other
    cross-site tracking opt-out signals, because it does not engage in cross-site tracking or
    behavioral advertising in the first place. We will note the date of any material change to this
    policy at the top of this page.
  </p>

  <h2>International visitors</h2>
  <p>
    This website is operated from, and primarily intended for visitors in, the United States. If
    you access this site from outside the United States, your information may be transferred to
    and processed in the United States or other countries where our service providers operate,
    which may have different data protection laws than your home country.
  </p>

  <h2>Changes to this policy</h2>
  <p>
    We may update this Privacy Policy from time to time. Material changes will be reflected by
    updating the effective date at the top of this page. We encourage you to review this page
    periodically.
  </p>

  <h2>Contact us</h2>
  <p>
    Questions about this Privacy Policy, or requests regarding your information, can be sent to <a href={`mailto:${email}`}>{email}</a>.
  </p>
</LegalPage>
